[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   TEP / Planet-9 -- step b5: the sample's own discovery footprint
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   The last open loophole in the bias discussion (step b1) is that
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   the detached objects may have been discovered by surveys whose
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   combined footprint was narrower than the generic control
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   footprint -- the "targeted pointing" channel.  This step
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   reconstructs the *actual* discovery footprint of the 44 detached
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   objects from real metadata rather than assuming one.
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   Every provisional designation encodes its own discovery epoch:
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   (YYYY Lx) -> the letter gives the half-month of discovery
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   (A = Jan 1-15, B = Jan 16-31, ... Y = Dec 16-31; I skipped).
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   An object found in a given half-month was, with high
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   probability, found near opposition: its discovery ecliptic
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   longitude lies within ~+-60-90 deg of the opposition longitude
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   lam_opp = lam_sun + 180 on that date.  The distribution of
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   lam_opp across the sample IS the true discovery footprint --
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   measured, not modeled.
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   F1  The footprint itself: R(lam_opp) and its distribution.
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   If the extreme-TNO discoveries came from a narrow seasonal
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   window, R(lam_opp) is large and the pointing channel can in
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   principle reach the observed R(varpi) = 0.33.
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   F2  Realized coupling: varpi - lam_opp per object vs the OSSOS
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   benchmark (mean |dphi| ~ 51 deg).
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   F3  The exact ceiling test: under the strongest possible
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   pointing model every object's perihelion direction equals
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   its discovery longitude, so R(varpi)_max = R(lam_opp) --
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   a hard bound computed on the real footprint, not a proxy.
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   Then the realistic version: varpi_i ~ VM(lam_opp_i, kappa)
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   for a fraction f of objects, uniform otherwise, with
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   kappa calibrated to the OSSOS |dphi| distribution --
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   does the TRUE footprint + measured coupling reproduce
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   the cluster?
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   F4  Comparison against the generic control footprint
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   (control-pool Omega marginal): is the detached discovery
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   footprint actually narrower than the generic one?
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   Caveats: lam_opp is a proxy for discovery longitude (objects
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   can be found up to ~90 deg off opposition, smearing the true
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   footprint further -- which only widens it, making the ceiling
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   argument conservative in the direction that matters).
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   first_observation precoveries are not discovery events; the
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   designation date is the discovery epoch.
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   Outputs: results/step_b5_discovery_footprint.json,
[2026-09-20 10:42:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 014]   figures/supplementary/step_b5_discovery_footprint.png
